 "answer_verbatim": "A good place to start is **ATA Martial Arts – St. Peters**, especially if you’re looking for a structured program for younger kids. It lists separate classes for **ages 4–6** and **7–12**, with an emphasis on focus, confidence, discipline, and self-defense.\n\n- **Address:** 6720 Mexico Rd, St. Peters, MO 63376  \n- **Phone:** (636) 556-5271  \n- **Website:** [atastpeters.com](https://www.atastpeters.com/our-classes)\n\nIf your child is more interested in grappling, **Onyx Grappling** offers kids’ Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu at **953 Jungermann Road**; call **(636) 339-4277** to ask about age groups and a trial class.\n\nI’d visit a class before enrolling and see how the instructor handles kids, whether beginners feel included, and whether the schedule and total costs work for your family.",
